        <customTabListAdditionalFields>CONTACT.PHONE1</customTabListAdditionalFields>
        <!--
            ⚠ ADDED 2026-08-21 (post-deploy UX request) - hide standard list-view buttons so
            "Add Investor & Investing Entity" is the only action IR users see on the Contact list
            view. Best-effort per known excludedStandardButtons values for this platform feature -
            NOT independently verified against this org's exact accepted enum (no
            salesforce-api-context MCP or web search available this session).

            ⚠ REWORKED 2026-08-21 (validation round correction) - the bare token `New` was
            REJECTED: "No such standard button to exclude New". Standard objects use
            OBJECT-SPECIFIC button names in searchLayouts (pattern: NewAccount, NewContact,
            NewLead, ...), not the generic label shown in the UI - corrected to `NewContact`
            (high confidence, directly matches the documented per-object naming pattern).
            Validation is SERIAL (same behavior observed throughout this whole change's flow
            work) - PrintableListView had not yet been tested when `New` failed, so it is LEFT
            AS-IS (not proven wrong, not proven right either) rather than guessed at a modified
            token with no better alternative to offer.
            `Import` was DROPPED ENTIRELY, NOT reworked - genuine low confidence on the correct
            object-specific token (could plausibly be `Import`, `ImportContacts`, `ContactImport`,
            or something else entirely) and, per instruction, hiding Import is a nice-to-have, not
            worth a further validation round on a guess. If Import should still be hidden, that is
            an open follow-up requiring the correct token to be confirmed (e.g. via Setup UI
            inspection or a future salesforce-api-context lookup), not attempted here.
              - NewContact: the standard "New Contact" button. High confidence.
              - PrintableListView: the "Printable View" button visible in the user's screenshot.
              Unvalidated (masked by the New error until this round) - moderate-high confidence,
              left unchanged, no better alternative token identified.
            NOT ATTEMPTED: "Intelligence View" (also visible in the screenshot) - this is very
            likely NOT a `excludedStandardButtons`-controllable standard button at all, but a
            separate List View Intelligence / Einstein feature toggle controlled at the org/Setup
            level, unrelated to SearchLayouts. Flagging this explicitly rather than guessing at a
            token for it - if it needs to be hidden, that is a different mechanism (Setup >
            Einstein / List View settings) outside this file's scope.
            🔴 BLAST RADIUS: SearchLayouts is ORG-WIDE PER OBJECT, NOT PER-PROFILE. Excluding
            NewContact here removes that button from EVERY Contact list view for EVERY user in
            the org, not just IR users - Acquisitions, Transactions, Property Management, etc. all
            lose the ability to create a Contact via the list-view "New" button (record creation
            via other paths - e.g. New from a related list, or the object Home page - is
            unaffected). If this proves too broad, revert by removing the excludedStandardButtons
            block below; it does not require touching any other file.
        -->
        <excludedStandardButtons>NewContact</excludedStandardButtons>
        <excludedStandardButtons>PrintableListView</excludedStandardButtons>
        <listViewButtons>Add_Investor_Investing_Entity</listViewButtons>
        <lookupDialogsAdditionalFields>FULL_NAME</lookupDialogsAdditionalFields>
        <lookupDialogsAdditionalFields>ACCOUNT.NAME</lookupDialogsAdditionalFields>
        <lookupDialogsAdditionalFields>ACCOUNT.SITE</lookupDialogsAdditionalFields>
        <!--
            ⚠ TRIMMED 2026-08-21 (check-only validation fix) - this block originally carried 11
            lookupPhoneDialogsAdditionalFields entries; the platform allows a maximum of 10
            ("No more than 10 columns may be specified in lookupPhoneDialogsAdditionalFields").
            This was pre-existing retrieved boilerplate that had never actually been deployed
            before, so the defect stayed latent until this change's deploy touched the file.
            ACCOUNT.PHONE2 was removed as the least informative entry in a phone-dialog lookup
            context - Account phone coverage is preserved via ACCOUNT.PHONE1, and all six Contact
            phone fields (PHONE1-6) were kept intact since those are the actual point of a
            phone-number lookup dialog.
        -->
        <lookupPhoneDialogsAdditionalFields>FULL_NAME</lookupPhoneDialogsAdditionalFields>
        <lookupPhoneDialogsAdditionalFields>ACCOUNT.NAME</lookupPhoneDialogsAdditionalFields>
        <lookupPhoneDialogsAdditionalFields>ACCOUNT.SITE</lookupPhoneDialogsAdditionalFields>
        <lookupPhoneDialogsAdditionalFields>CONTACT.PHONE1</lookupPhoneDialogsAdditionalFields>
        <lookupPhoneDialogsAdditionalFields>CONTACT.PHONE2</lookupPhoneDialogsAdditionalFields>
        <lookupPhoneDialogsAdditionalFields>CONTACT.PHONE3</lookupPhoneDialogsAdditionalFields>
        <lookupPhoneDialogsAdditionalFields>CONTACT.PHONE4</lookupPhoneDialogsAdditionalFields>
        <lookupPhoneDialogsAdditionalFields>CONTACT.PHONE5</lookupPhoneDialogsAdditionalFields>
        <lookupPhoneDialogsAdditionalFields>CONTACT.PHONE6</lookupPhoneDialogsAdditionalFields>
        <lookupPhoneDialogsAdditionalFields>ACCOUNT.PHONE1</lookupPhoneDialogsAdditionalFields>
        <searchResultsAdditionalFields>FULL_NAME</searchResultsAdditionalFields>
        <searchResultsAdditionalFields>ACCOUNT.NAME</searchResultsAdditionalFields>
        <searchResultsAdditionalFields>ACCOUNT.SITE</searchResultsAdditionalFields>
        <searchResultsAdditionalFields>CONTACT.PHONE1</searchResultsAdditionalFields>
        <searchResultsAdditionalFields>CONTACT.EMAIL</searchResultsAdditionalFields>
